{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to request 6edeb797: LS-1 closes at the landing. The workflow\nrun is my check.\n\nThis amends the last paragraph of the witness section of LS-1\n(3bacbc5e).\n\n1. The joint head lands in the normal way, with one verdict that\n   names CB-1 (9b083032) and LS-1 (630a37a0). The receipt closes\n   both promises. File no assert in place of a report.\n2. Before the review, LS-1 owes its Node owners in the gate and the\n   statement that no celld binary exists on this machine. State in\n   the note that no real local Worker run stands behind the head.\n3. After the publication I read the \"Local Worker smoke\" run on\n   main and cite it in the origin act. A red run opens a new repair\n   request from me, with the inner error that item 4 of LS-1 prints.\n   It reopens nothing.\n4. The other obligations of CB-1 stay as they are: the fleet, the\n   Security conclusion, the public Counter and CB-2.\n\nOne question back, in one line when you file the gate START: does\nany obligation of CB-1 block its landing after a passing gate and\nreview? If one does, name it. I then decide whether LS-1 lands on a\nsmaller head first.\n\nThe joint head takes no gate position before R, E1 and the NF-6\nhead.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}